  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal, by reason of the poor and cramped layout of the ground floor flats , poor outlook to living spaces for each flat, would result in a poor standard of living accommodation for future occupiers of those flats, to the detriment of their residential amenities,&amp;nbsp; contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policies D6 and D3, (D.7 and D.10) of The London Plan (2021), Policies DM1 and DM26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), The Mayor of London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance (2016), the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010) and Housing Design Standards LPG (2023).&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal, by reason of the poor vertical stacking arrangement between kitchen/living areas and bedrooms would result in a poor standard of living accommodation for future occupiers of flat 1, to the detriment of their residential amenities,&amp;nbsp; contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policies D6 and D3, (D.7 and D.10) of The London Plan (2021), Policies DM1 and DM26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), The Mayor of London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance (2016), the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010) and Housing Design Standards LPG (2023).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal, would fail to provide private amenity space for the upper floor flat 3 resulting in a poor standard of living accommodation for future occupiers of this flat, to the detriment of their residential amenities,&amp;nbsp; contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policies D6 and D3, (D.7 and D.10) of The London Plan (2021), Policies DM1 and DM26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), The Mayor of London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance (2016), the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010) and Housing Design Standards LPG (2023).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal, by reason of the lack of side access to the rear garden would result in the refuse and waste recycling bins and bicycle stores, being located in the front garden area, resulting in a cluttered and poor quality environment to the detriment of the character and appearance of the subject property and the streetscene, contrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Core Policy CS.1B, Policies D3.D11 and T5 of the London Plan (2021), Policies DM 1, DM 26, DM42 and DM45 of the Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010)&amp;nbsp;and Housing Design Standards LPG (2023).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
